---
/**
 * Founding-engineer job description and application. Posts to the Netlify
 * form "job-application". The copy follows the "Job Description" section of
 * the founders' job-description Google Doc; keep the two in sync.
 */
import ApplicationPage from "../components/ApplicationPage.astro";
import FormField from "../components/FormField.astro";

const areas = [
    {
        name: "Programming languages",
        example:
            "Designed a language or type system; built a type checker, interpreter, or language tooling used by others",
    },
    {
        name: "Compilers",
        example:
            "Built IRs, optimization passes, or code generation for a production compiler",
    },
    {
        name: "Databases",
        example:
            "Built a query engine, optimizer, storage layer, or transaction system",
    },
    {
        name: "Distributed systems",
        example:
            "Built replication or consensus infrastructure that runs at scale",
    },
];
---

<ApplicationPage
    title="Founding engineer"
    description="Cambra is hiring founding engineers to build the language and runtime end to end. Fully remote, $225,000 plus founding engineer equity."
    formName="job-application"
    heading="Founding engineer"
    submitLabel="Apply"
    layout="stacked"
>
    <Fragment slot="intro">
        <h2>About Cambra</h2>
        <p>
            Cambra is building a unified programming platform that fuses the
            application runtime and the database into one system.
        </p>
        <p>
            It presents like a programming language, while the runtime handles
            durability, distribution, and fault tolerance. The goal is one
            system that spans transactional, analytical, and streaming
            workloads, so you stop stitching together an app server, a database,
            a warehouse, and a stream processor.
        </p>
        <p>
            Cambra is{" "}
            <a href="https://github.com/cambra-dev/cambra">open source</a>. Your
            work will be public from day one.
        </p>

        <h2>The team</h2>
        <p>
            The founders, Dan Sotolongo (CEO), Daniel Mills, and Skylar Cook,
            have worked together for over a decade. Dan and Daniel scaled a
            database product to $100M ARR at Snowflake.
        </p>
        <p>
            We raised a seed round led by Lightspeed. You'd be one of the first
            engineers, shaping the system's core design and the engineering
            culture around it.
        </p>

        <h2>The role</h2>
        <p>
            You'll build the Cambra language and runtime end to end. You bring
            deep expertise in one area, and you'll work across component
            boundaries. The work spans:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Language:</strong> syntax, semantics, and the type
                system that make durable, distributed code feel ordinary
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Compiler:</strong> the IR, analyses, and optimizations
                that lower programs onto the runtime
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Query and storage:</strong> planning, execution, and
                storage for transactional, analytical, and streaming workloads
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Distributed runtime:</strong> durability, replication,
                and fault tolerance, invisible to the programmer
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            There is no fixed lane. Priorities shift as the system takes shape,
            and each founding engineer will own major pieces of it.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we're looking for</h2>
        <p>
            We're hiring people who have pushed forward the state of the art in
            at least one of these areas, and want to do it again:
        </p>
        <ul>
            {areas.map((a) => (
                <li>
                    <strong>{a.name}:</strong> {a.example}
                </li>
            ))}
        </ul>
        <p>You also:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Work well in a group.</strong> You share context freely,
                take and give hard feedback, and care about the team's output
                more than your own.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Wield coding agents fluently.</strong> You use them
                daily and know where they speed you up and where they don't.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Want to reach beyond your specialty.</strong> You're
                excited to learn the other three areas from teammates who are
                experts in them.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How we work</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Fully remote.</strong> 4 working hours during US Mountain
                Time business hours required daily.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Quarterly offsites.</strong> We meet in person in the US
                every 3 months; attendance is required.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Agent-native.</strong> Coding agents are a core part of
                how we build, not an experiment.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Compensation</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Salary:</strong> $225,000
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Equity:</strong> founding engineer equity; we share
                specifics in the first conversation.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Benefits:</strong> health coverage, a
                home-office/equipment budget, and travel covered for offsites.
                We hire internationally.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How to apply</h2>
        <p>
            Fill in the form below with your résumé, a few lines about your
            relevant experience, and a link to work you're proud of (code,
            papers, talks, or a project write-up).
        </p>
    </Fragment>

    <FormField name="name" label="Name" required />
    <FormField name="email" label="Email" type="email" required />
    <FormField name="location" label="Where are you based?" required />
    <FormField
        name="hours"
        label="Can you work 4 hours a day during US Mountain Time business hours, and attend a US offsite every 3 months?"
        type="select"
        required
        options={["Yes", "No", "Let's discuss"]}
    />
    <FormField
        name="resume"
        label="Résumé link"
        type="url"
        required
        placeholder="https://"
    />
    <FormField
        name="area"
        label="Where have you pushed the state of the art?"
        type="select"
        required
        options={[...areas.map((a) => a.name), "Something else"]}
    />
    <FormField
        name="experience"
        label="A few lines about your relevant experience"
        type="textarea"
        required
    />
    <FormField
        name="work"
        label="A link to work you're proud of"
        type="url"
        required
        hint="Code, papers, talks, or a project write-up."
        placeholder="https://"
    />
    <FormField name="links" label="GitHub, LinkedIn, or personal site" />
</ApplicationPage>
